\ term.fr — terminal control for fr, written in fr. The substrate a self-hosted
\ ember needs: ANSI escape output (cursor, colour, clear) and termios raw mode via
\ the kernel's `syscall3` (ioctl). Load order mirrors the rest of the tooling:
\
\     ( cat prelude.fr term.fr yourtui.fr ) | ./fr
\
\ Depends on prelude.fr (u. invert 1+ ...). Together with `key` (prelude), `see`
\ and `trace` (prelude), this is everything the introspection + I/O sides of an
\ fr-native ember need; what's left is the TUI layout/loop itself.
\
\ NOTE: every escape is emitted byte-by-byte through `emit`/`u.`, i.e. one write(2)
\ per byte. Correct but flickery; a redraw should buffer into a string and `type`
\ it in one syscall. That buffering is a deliberate later optimization (see ROADMAP).

\ --- ANSI escape sequences ---------------------------------------------------
\ CSI = ESC '[' . All sequences are ESC '[' <params> <final-byte>.
: esc  ( -- )   27 emit ;
: csi  ( -- )   esc [char] [ emit ;

: clear ( -- )  csi [char] 2 emit [char] J emit  csi [char] H emit ;  \ wipe + home
: home  ( -- )  csi [char] H emit ;                                   \ cursor to 1,1
: at    ( row col -- )                  \ position the cursor (1-based row, col)
  csi swap u. [char] ; emit u. [char] H emit ;

\ SGR (Select Graphic Rendition): colours and styles. 0=reset, 1=bold,
\ 30..37 = foreground, 40..47 = background, +60 for the bright variants.
: sgr   ( n -- )   csi u. [char] m emit ;
: reset ( -- )     0 sgr ;
: bold  ( -- )     1 sgr ;
: fg    ( n -- )   30 + sgr ;           \ e.g.  3 fg  -> yellow text
: bg    ( n -- )   40 + sgr ;

: hide-cursor ( -- )  csi [char] ? emit [char] 2 emit [char] 5 emit [char] l emit ;
: show-cursor ( -- )  csi [char] ? emit [char] 2 emit [char] 5 emit [char] h emit ;

\ --- termios raw mode, via ioctl(2) ------------------------------------------
\ ioctl is syscall 16: ioctl(fd, request, argp). The kernel `struct termios` for
\ TCGETS/TCSETS is 36 bytes; we over-allocate. We toggle cbreak mode — clear
\ ICANON (line buffering) and ECHO in c_lflag (offset 12) — so `key` returns each
\ keystroke immediately and silently. (Not full raw: we leave signals/CR mapping
\ alone, which is what a key-driven TUI actually wants.)
16    constant SYS_ioctl
21505 constant TCGETS         \ 0x5401  — read current termios
21506 constant TCSETS         \ 0x5402  — set termios now
21523 constant TIOCGWINSZ     \ 0x5413  — get window size
10    constant ICANON|ECHO    \ ICANON (2) | ECHO (8) — both live in c_lflag's low bits

variable termbuf  56 allot    \ working termios struct (need 36; pad to be safe)
variable saved-lflag          \ original c_lflag, to restore exactly on raw-off

: tcget ( -- )   0 TCGETS termbuf SYS_ioctl syscall3 drop ;
: tcset ( -- )   0 TCSETS termbuf SYS_ioctl syscall3 drop ;
: lflag ( -- a ) termbuf 12 + ;   \ address of the c_lflag cell within termbuf

: raw-on ( -- )                 \ enter cbreak mode (save the original first)
  tcget
  lflag @  saved-lflag !
  lflag  saved-lflag @  ICANON|ECHO invert and  swap !
  tcset ;
: raw-off ( -- )                \ restore the terminal exactly as we found it
  tcget
  lflag  saved-lflag @  swap !
  tcset ;

\ window size: struct winsize is { u16 rows, u16 cols, ... }; little-endian.
variable winbuf  8 allot
: u16@ ( a -- n )   dup c@  swap 1+ c@  256 * + ;   \ read a little-endian 2-byte field
: term-size ( -- rows cols )
  0 TIOCGWINSZ winbuf SYS_ioctl syscall3 drop
  winbuf u16@   winbuf 2 + u16@ ;

\ --- a tiny composition demo (proves the pieces fit together) ----------------
\ paint: position the cursor, set a foreground colour, in one word.
: paint ( row col colour -- )   >r at r> fg ;
